flowchart TB
    accTitle: Scopegate logical application boundaries
    accDescr: A modular application owns HTTP, use cases and background processes around one primary database. Local adapters are implemented; live provider and host integration remain separate.
    browser[React workspace<br/>Typed HTTP and scoped query cache]
    subgraph app[One versioned application boundary]
        http[FastAPI HTTP transport<br/>Session or distinct machine principal]
        services[Cohesive application services<br/>Identity · access · enrollment · catalog · migration]
        policy[Pure resource-use policy<br/>Immutable facts and decision time]
        transaction[SQLAlchemy Core transaction boundary<br/>Ordered locks · receipts · audit]
        worker[Separate delivery worker process<br/>Lease claim and acknowledgment]
        cli[Opt-in operations CLI<br/>Reviewed migration and recovery]
        http --> services
        services --> policy
        services --> transaction
        cli --> services
        worker --> transaction
    end
    database[(Primary PostgreSQL<br/>Authority · audit · outbox · migration)]
    identity[Independent local OIDC<br/>Verified provider claims]
    mailbox[Local mailbox adapter<br/>Postcommit delivery]
    journal[Local durable journal adapter<br/>Intent before transaction · outcome after]
    browser -->|Same-origin cookie and CSRF| http
    http -->|Configured OIDC exchange| identity
    transaction -->|One service-owned commit| database
    worker -->|Outside database transaction| mailbox
    services -->|Outside domain locks| journal
    classDef core fill:#f0fdfa,stroke:#0f766e,color:#134e4a;
    classDef adapter fill:#eff6ff,stroke:#2563eb,color:#172554;
    classDef authority fill:#0f172a,stroke:#0f172a,color:#ffffff;
    class http,services,policy,transaction,worker,cli core;
    class browser,identity,mailbox,journal adapter;
    class database authority;
